I've been playing this game on and off since the PC Hack days, but I'm
still pretty terrible at it.  I've only made it to the quest once
(Tourist), but died pretty quickly there.  I've never made it to the
castle, etc. either.  I've gotten some good tips via this newsgroup,
spoilers, etc; most recently the "Ascensions, anyone?" thread.  Most
of the time, I had only played Tourists, but in the last year I've
been playing Orc Wizards.

Anyway, if I could get some advice specific to Orc Wizards, I would
appreciate it.  I pick Orcs partly for the oddness, but I also think
the starting poison resistance makes-up for the max 16 INT - my Orc
Wizards rarely starve.  Here's my basic strategy at this point:

* Try to get a dagger for a primary weapon ASAP to start building that
weapon skill.  Often this means killing a friendly goblin - otherwise
I can usually get some in the Gnomish Mines.

* Do the first couple of levels of the Gnomish Mines for the daggers,
tools, and experience, but don't try to complete it yet.  If I am
doing well, I will try to make it to Minetown for the altar, in case
it happens to be co-aligned.

* Once I find an altar that is co-aligned or convertible, try to
sacrifice for Magicbane.

* If I get a wish, I ask for silver dragon scale mail first.  I'm
undecided as to what the best second wish should be

I've only had enough money at the Minetown altar to buy protection
once so far.

Any tips on survivability, making money, or getting AC down other than
protection or wishing for dragon scale mail (without impeding
spellcasting)?


